From: Lecithin <noreply@lophinelabs.invalid>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 14:40:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] answer getRespawnLocation from any tick thread

CraftPlayer#getRespawnLocation(true) resolves the RESPAWN world from the
player's persisted respawn data and then validates the spawn block in it:

  ServerLevel world = server.getLevel(respawnData.dimension());
  ServerPlayer.findRespawnAndUseSpawnBlock(world, respawnConfig, false)
    -> world.getBlockState(pos)
    -> Level#getCurrentWorldData()

getCurrentWorldData() resolves world data from whatever region this thread is
currently ticking and then asserts identity with the level being read. The
respawn world comes from stored data and is unrelated to either end of whatever
the caller is doing, so the assertion fails whenever a player's bed is in a
different world from the one whose region is ticking - and it throws
IllegalStateException out of the plugin, not a diagnostic.
CraftOfflinePlayer#getRespawnLocation(true) does the same thing from the same
stored data, so it is guarded here too.

That is the common case, not an exotic one. A cross-world move fires
PlayerChangedWorldEvent on the destination region, and reading a player's bed
spawn from that handler is a standard Paper idiom - directly, or through
PaperLib.getBedSpawnLocationAsync, whose handler on this version is
BedSpawnLocationSync and calls straight through on the calling thread (PaperLib's
version regex takes a single digit for the major version, so on 26.2 it parses 0
and every isVersion check is false - an upstream defect that misfires the same
way on stock Paper).

Ask first whether this thread may read the respawn world there, using the
platform's own TickThread.isTickThreadFor, and validate only when it may. When
it may not, return the stored location - which is exactly what the sibling
overload getRespawnLocation(false) already returns. So on a thread that owns a
region no ownership check is disabled, bypassed or swallowed; nothing is loaded,
nothing is dispatched to another region or to the global scheduler, and the
calling thread never waits.

Tick threads only, deliberately. A thread that is not a tick thread at all - a
plugin's own async pool - keeps upstream's hard failure, because there the
exception is the async catcher doing its job rather than a regionisation
artefact; answering it would delete a real diagnostic. This is the same line
LecithinCrossRegionBlockRead draws.

The shutdown thread is checked directly rather than through isTickThreadFor,
which is not usable there: with no current region it returns isShutdownThread(),
i.e. true for every chunk in every world, which would send the validating read
through to throw World mismatch anyway - or to dereference a null
RegionizedWorldData, since RegionShutdownThread exposes none while its
shuttingDown region is unset, and that is precisely the window in which
PlayerQuitEvent and plugin onDisable run. The read is allowed there only when a
region of this same level is the one shutting down, and only for positions it
covers.

The bounded difference, stated rather than hidden: on the fallback path the
answer is not validated, so a bed broken since the player last slept in it is
reported instead of null. That is strictly better than throwing, which aborts
the caller entirely. It is NOT strictly better than null: the fallback returns
the raw stored block coordinate - the integer corner of the bed or anchor block,
with no centring, no safety scan and no chunk load - so a plugin doing
player.teleport(player.getRespawnLocation()) can put the player inside a block,
where null would have sent them to world spawn. The trade is an unvalidated and
possibly unsafe location in exchange for a call that completes at all. It cannot
be improved on synchronously, because validating would mean blocking a region
tick on another region's chunk.

And the fallback is the common path, not an edge case: a bed in another world
can never be validated from a region of this one, and neither can a bed in a
region of this world that this thread does not own or whose chunks are not
loaded. Every cross-world respawn lookup - the case this exists for - takes it.

Grouped by API symbol, not by plugin: the gap is Player#getRespawnLocation and
OfflinePlayer#getRespawnLocation, and no plugin name, jar hash or library name
appears anywhere. Kill switch: compat-config.respawn-location-lookup=false.

diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftOfflinePlayer.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftOfflinePlayer.java
index 1aa8f1e0a3093a8b9e77213c56f987cd6ca7df86..9afdae1115f7c2bbb9a644f62c2cead783817565 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftOfflinePlayer.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/CraftOfflinePlayer.java
@@ -375,7 +375,14 @@ public class CraftOfflinePlayer implements OfflinePlayer, ConfigurationSerializa
         final ServerLevel level = this.server.console.getLevel(respawnConfig.respawnData().dimension());
         if (level == null) return null;
 
-        if (!loadLocationAndValidate) {
+        // Lecithin start - validating reads the respawn world's blocks, which the caller may not own.
+        // The respawn world comes from stored data and is unrelated to the region this thread is
+        // ticking, so on any other region getCurrentWorldData() throws World mismatch out of the
+        // caller - Bukkit.getOfflinePlayer(uuid).getRespawnLocation(true) is reachable from every
+        // region thread and from the shutdown thread. Fall back to the stored location, which is
+        // what the sibling getRespawnLocation(false) already returns.
+        if (!loadLocationAndValidate || !fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinRespawnLocationLookup.canValidate(level, respawnConfig.respawnData().pos())) {
+        // Lecithin end
             return CraftLocation.toBukkit(respawnConfig.respawnData().pos(), level, respawnConfig.respawnData().yaw(), respawnConfig.respawnData().pitch());
         }
 
diff --git a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftPlayer.java b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftPlayer.java
index e0f667b680aeba37d83cc225ec624ca4fd168038..1844205bd7f46b0d64bfeec7593e3d8e466544b2 100644
--- a/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftPlayer.java
+++ b/src/main/java/org/bukkit/craftbukkit/entity/CraftPlayer.java
@@ -1418,7 +1418,13 @@ public class CraftPlayer extends CraftHumanEntity implements Player, PluginMessa
         final ServerLevel world = this.server.getServer().getLevel(respawnData.dimension());
         if (world == null) return null;
 
-        if (!loadLocationAndValidate) {
+        // Lecithin start - validating reads the respawn world's blocks, which the caller may not own.
+        // The respawn world comes from stored data and is unrelated to the region this thread is
+        // ticking, so on any other region getCurrentWorldData() throws World mismatch out of the
+        // caller - notably out of a PlayerChangedWorldEvent handler asking for a player's bed spawn.
+        // Fall back to the stored location, which is what getRespawnLocation(false) already returns.
+        if (!loadLocationAndValidate || !fun.bm.lecithin.compat.LecithinRespawnLocationLookup.canValidate(world, respawnData.pos())) {
+        // Lecithin end
             return CraftLocation.toBukkit(respawnData.pos(), world, respawnData.yaw(), respawnData.pitch());
         }
 
